{"name":"Fireside","hex":"#6e4a44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fireside","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The area near a domestic fire or hearth.","One's home."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireside"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fireplace","blocks":[{"text":"A fireplace or hearth is a structure made of brick, stone or metal designed to contain a fire. Fireplaces are used to heat a room or dwelling and also for the relaxing ambiance they create. Modern fireplaces vary in heat efficiency, depending on the design."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Open_fireplace_with_icon.jpg/330px-Open_fireplace_with_icon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireplace","wikidata":"Q188669"},{"title":"Fireside (LDS Church)","blocks":[{"text":"A fireside is a supplementary meeting in the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, often held in the evening."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireside_(LDS_Church)","wikidata":"Q5451952"},{"title":"Fireside (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Fireside is a Swedish rock band that formed in the Swedish hardcore scene in the early 1990s. After finding moderate success as a post-grunge/alternative rock band, yet tiring of playing half-filled venues, Fireside adopted an emo/pop punk sound in 1998. In 2000, with the release of Elite, the band took a more experimental approach to rock, but 2003's All You Had saw the band shift towards garage rock."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireside_(band)","wikidata":"Q472171"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Outdoor_Fireplace.JPG/500px-Outdoor_Fireplace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Outdoor_Fireplace.JPG/1280px-Outdoor_Fireplace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con